@startuml
title III-04 - Feedback for a product in a completed order

autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Customer
boundary "Customer Portal" as Web
control "Feedback API" as API
database "CRM Database" as DB

Customer -> Web: Select purchased product; enter rating and comment
Web -> API: POST /api/products/{productId}/feedback\n(JWT, orderId, rating, comment)
API -> API: Require Customer identity; validate rating 1-5\nand optional comment up to 4000 characters
alt Invalid identity or input
  API --> Web: Authentication/validation error
else Authenticated Customer
  API -> DB: Lock order by orderId and check ownership
  alt Order not owned or product absent from order
    API --> Web: 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND
  else Order is not COMPLETED
    API --> Web: 403 RECEIPT_REQUIRED
  else Completed order contains product
    API -> DB: Check existing feedback for order_id and product_id
    alt Feedback already exists
      API --> Web: 409 DUPLICATE_FEEDBACK
    else First feedback for this order/product
      API -> DB: Save feedback with order_id, customer_id, product_id\nrating, content and status=NEW
      DB --> API: Feedback created
      API --> Web: 201 FeedbackView
      Web --> Customer: Show submitted review
    end
  end
end
note over API,DB
  Only COMPLETED orders grant review eligibility.
  UNIQUE(order_id, product_id) protects each purchased product per order.
  Another completed order may have another review for the same product.
end note
@enduml
